--- compose.next.yaml: api service has no bind-mounted volumes (upload dir is container-local, ephemeral, not host-exposed) ---
(no 'volumes:' key under the api service)

Conclusion: default is the relative path './var/import', resolved against the image WORKDIR
/app (backend/Dockerfile), so it lands at /app/var/import purely inside the api container's
own filesystem. No KIVVI_IMPORT_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY override is set in compose.next.yaml and the
api service declares no volumes, so this path is never bind-mounted to the host or a named
volume -- a safe, self-contained default. Filename handling (ImportUploadStorage.store) strips
client path components (basename()) and generates a random 32-hex stored name, so client input
never reaches the filesystem path directly (traversal-safe).
